{% comment %}
  Renders the string "true" when a product is flagged "coming soon", nothing otherwise.

  A "coming soon" product behaves exactly like a sold-out one — price replaced,
  add-to-cart disabled — but reads "Coming soon" and is never dimmed. The tag
  match lives here alone so the rule has one home.

  Matched tags (case-insensitive): "coming-soon", "coming soon".

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object

  Usage — capture the render, then test it with `contains` so stray whitespace
  can never flip the result:
    {%- capture coming_soon %}{% render 'coming-soon', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- if coming_soon contains 'true' -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign coming_soon_tags = product.tags | join: ',' | downcase
  if coming_soon_tags contains 'coming-soon' or coming_soon_tags contains 'coming soon'
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
